How to start either the Single Editor or Multi-Editor versions:\
\
Starting Multi-Editor:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 \cb1 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 If Single Editor is already on\'a08001, start Multi on\'a08000:
\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 cd "/Users/charlesvaughn/Desktop/VScode_Test/PythonDB4-3-26"\
source .venv/bin/activate\
CONTACTSFREESHARE_USE_APP_DATA=1 \\\
python3 run_local.py\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Then open\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://127.0.0.1:8000/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 http://127.0.0.1:8000}}\'a0for Multi. Single stays at\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://127.0.0.1:8001/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 http://127.0.0.1:8001}}.\
If port 8000 is already taken (Single was started there), check with:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 lsof -nP -iTCP:8000 -sTCP:LISTEN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Quit that Single process first, or keep Single on 8001 and use the commands above.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth0 \
\ul Starting Single Editor:\ulnone \
Multi-Editor is already using\'a0
\f4\fs27 \cf6 \cb7 http://127.0.0.1:8000
\f3\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 , so start Single Editor from its own folder and keep its data separate.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b \cf2 \cb3 From Terminal
\f3\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs24 \cf8 \cb9 cd\cf2  \cf10 "/Users/charlesvaughn/Desktop/CFS Single Editor"\cf2 \cb1 \
\cf8 \cb9 source\cf2  \cf10 .venv/bin/activate\cf2 \cb1 \
\cb9 CONTACTSFREESHARE_DATA_DIR=\cf10 "\cf11 $HOME\cf10 /ContactsFreeShare-SingleEditor"\cf2  \cf8 \\\cf2 \cb1 \
\cb9 CONTACTSFREESHARE_UPDATE_MANIFEST_URL=\cf10 "https://menfisher.github.io/contactsfreeshare-se-updates/app_update_manifest.json"\cf2  \cf12 \\\cf2 \cb1 \
\cb9 python3 \cf10 run_local.py\cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs30 \cf2 \cb7 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Then open\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://127.0.0.1:8000/"}}{\fldrslt 
\f6 \cf6 http://127.0.0.1:8000}}.\cb1 \
\cb3 If Multi is still running, that address will stay Multi. Quit Multi first, or start Single on another port (for example\'a0
\f4\fs27 \cb7 8001
\f3\fs30 \cb3 ) and open that URL instead.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs27 \cf2 \cb7 CONTACTSFREESHARE_DATA_DIR
\f3\fs30 \cb3 \'a0matters: without it, Single uses the same\'a0
\f4\fs27 \cb7 ~/Library/Application Support/ContactsFreeShare
\f3\fs30 \cb3 \'a0folder as Multi.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f5\b \cf2 \cb3 Packaged 1.221 (optional)
\f3\b0 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 Double-click\'a0
\f4\fs27 \cb7 Start ContactsFreeShare.command
\f3\fs30 \cb3 \'a0in:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs27 \cf2 \cb7 /Users/charlesvaughn/Desktop/CFS Single Editor/dist/ContactsFreeShare
\f3\fs30 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 That packaged launcher also wants port 8000 and the shared Application Support folder, so do not use it while Multi is running.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb9 How do I start Single on another port 8001 if Multi is already running\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs27 \cf6 \cb7 run_local.py
\f3\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 \'a0always binds\'a0
\f5\b 8000
\f3\b0 , so start Single with uvicorn on\'a0
\f5\b 8001
\f3\b0 \'a0instead. Keep Multi on 8000.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs24 \cf8 \cb9 cd\cf2  \cf10 "/Users/charlesvaughn/Desktop/CFS Single Editor"\cf2 \cb1 \
\cf8 \cb9 source\cf2  \cf10 .venv/bin/activate\cf2 \cb1 \
\cb9 CONTACTSFREESHARE_DATA_DIR=\cf10 "\cf11 $HOME\cf10 /ContactsFreeShare-SingleEditor"\cf2  \cf8 \\\cf2 \cb1 \
\cb9 CONTACTSFREESHARE_UPDATE_MANIFEST_URL=\cf10 "https://menfisher.github.io/contactsfreeshare-se-updates/app_update_manifest.json"\cf2  \cf12 \\\cf2 \cb1 \
\cb9 GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=\cf10 "http://127.0.0.1:8001/google/connect/callback"\cf2  \cf12 \\\cf2 \cb1 \
\cb9 APP_BASE_URL=\cf10 "http://127.0.0.1:8001"\cf2  \cf12 \\\cf2 \cb1 \
\cb9 python3 \cf11 -m\cf2  \cf10 uvicorn\cf2  \cf10 asgi:app\cf2  \cf11 --host\cf2  \cf13 127.0.0.1\cf2  \cf11 --port\cf2  \cf13 8001\cf2  \cf11 --reload\cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs30 \cf2 \cb7 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Then open\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://127.0.0.1:8001/"}}{\fldrslt 
\f6 \cf6 http://127.0.0.1:8001}}. Multi stays at\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://127.0.0.1:8000/"}}{\fldrslt 
\f6 \cf6 http://127.0.0.1:8000}}.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs27 \cf2 \cb7 CONTACTSFREESHARE_DATA_DIR
\f3\fs30 \cb3 \'a0keeps Single\'92s database out of Multi\'92s Application Support folder. If Google sign-in on Single fails, add\'a0
\f4\fs27 \cf6 \cb7 http://127.0.0.1:8001/google/connect/callback
\f3\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 \'a0as an authorized redirect URI in that Google Cloud OAuth client.\cb1 \
